1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,162
Stage Monitors.

2
00:00:02,112 --> 00:00:06,487
Learn Sends on Fader mode and how to respond to monitor requests.

3
00:00:06,487 --> 00:00:11,787
Stage monitors (wedges or in-ears) are completely separate from the main room mix.

4
00:00:11,787 --> 00:00:16,425
You can adjust someone's monitor without changing what the congregation hears.

5
00:00:16,425 --> 00:00:18,825
Using Sends on Fader.

6
00:00:18,825 --> 00:00:22,062
Press Sends on Fader button: It lights up.

7
00:00:22,062 --> 00:00:26,462
Left faders now control monitor sends, NOT the main room mix.

8
00:00:26,462 --> 00:00:33,862
Press SELECT on the monitor bus: On the right side, select which monitor mix you're adjusting (Bus 1, 2, etc.).

9
00:00:33,862 --> 00:00:39,862
Adjust the left faders: Each channel's fader now = how loud that source is in the selected monitor.

10
00:00:39,862 --> 00:00:41,737
Small moves.

11
00:00:41,737 --> 00:00:45,525
Press Sends on Fader again to EXIT: Light goes off.

12
00:00:45,525 --> 00:00:48,125
Faders go back to room mix.

13
00:00:48,125 --> 00:00:50,450
ALWAYS exit when done.

14
00:00:50,450 --> 00:00:57,700
⚠️ CRITICAL: If Sends on Fader is still lit and you think you're mixing the room, you're secretly changing someone's monitor.

15
00:00:57,700 --> 00:01:01,075
ALWAYS check that the button is off before mixing.

16
00:01:01,075 --> 00:01:04,062
Monitor Requests — Translations.

17
00:01:04,062 --> 00:01:09,637
When someone says I need more me., Raise their own mic or instrument in their personal monitor mix.

18
00:01:09,637 --> 00:01:14,912
When someone says I can't hear the keys., Raise the keyboard channel in their monitor mix.

19
00:01:14,912 --> 00:01:21,387
When someone says It's too loud in my monitor., Lower the loudest channel or pull the whole monitor bus down slightly.

20
00:01:21,387 --> 00:01:27,837
When someone says My monitor is ringing., Lower their OWN mic in their monitor mix — that's almost always the cause.

